  "interpretations": {
    "class_distribution": "Common_Rust is the largest class (1045 images, 31.2%) and Gray_Leaf_Spot the smallest (458, 13.7%), an imbalance ratio of 2.28:1. Without correction the model would under-predict Gray_Leaf_Spot, so training uses balanced class weights and we report macro-averaged precision/recall/F1 (every class counts equally) instead of relying on accuracy alone.",
    "color_index": "Median Green\u2212Red index from greenest to least green: Healthy (33.3), Blight (8.4), Common_Rust (8.2), Gray_Leaf_Spot (5.9). Healthy leaves keep the most chlorophyll; Gray_Leaf_Spot shows the strongest shift towards red/brown, consistent with necrotic (dead) tissue and rust-coloured pustules. Colour alone separates healthy from diseased leaves fairly well, but the overlapping distributions of the diseased classes show why the model also needs shape and texture.",
    "texture_contrast": "Median Laplacian variance from most to least textured: Common_Rust (975), Gray_Leaf_Spot (885), Blight (628), Healthy (266). High values mean many sharp edges, e.g. scattered pustules or small lesions; low values mean smoother surfaces or large uniform lesions. The wide, overlapping ranges also reflect differences in photo focus and background, which is why augmentation and a CNN that learns its own features are used rather than hand-made thresholds."
